{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985165-kindred-demographics-age-of-pcs","id":985165,"title":"Kindred Demographics + Age of PCs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-10T17:54:28-07:00","id":985165,"title":"Kindred Demographics + Age of PCs","content":"In Masquerade, kindred are ideally situated at 1:100,000 people but in many places there are as many as 1:10,000 people. Is there a number for Requiem?<br /> <br /> Also in Masquerade, the book suggests that PCs be no more than 25 years embraced. Is there a similar number for Requiem somewhere?<br /> <br /> I've been skimming through the first couple of chapters of Requiem 2e and I haven't been able to find anything. Maybe I should dig up 1e for guidance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:19:32-07:00","id":985177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Masquerade, kindred are ideally situated at 1:100,000 people but in many places there are as many as 1:10,000 people. Is there a number for Requiem? </div> </div> </div>Not really, Chronicles generally stays away from numbers like that so storytellers can decide for themselves based on what sort of plot they want to make. That said, Tokyo has around 350 kindred iirc, which means &quot;0.00256975036%&quot; of it's population are vampires.... which is really really small IMO.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also in Masquerade, the book suggests that PCs be no more than 25 years embraced. Is there a similar number for Requiem somewhere? </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. They're supposed to be rather young. Vampires who have &quot;been around the block&quot; get 5 starting xp so &quot;starting&quot; characters are newer than that, and 50-150 year old vamps have around 15 starting xp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-10-2016, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:19:36-07:00","id":985178,"title":"","content":"In first edition there was an adjustable ratio. Second accepts that 'whatever your story calls for' is appropriate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>First Edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">'In most small cities, the proportion of undead to mortals tends to be relatively low: One vampire per 100,000 or more mortals is not uncommon. In large cities, the ratio is usually nearer one vampire per 50,000 mortals. In some cities that seem to draw the Kindred for whatever reason - cities such as New York, London, New Orleans and Chicago - the ratio canbe substantially higher. Most Princes don't particularly keep track. As long as the population doesn't grow so high that people take notice of the predators among them, numbers don't matter.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding age, Blood Potency can help determine starting ages. But there's room for adjustment. You start at Blood Potency 1, but could have been a revenant or in torpor for eons. You get a point of Blood Potency every 50 years of being 'up.' Diablerie or experimentation can make it rise prematurely. I imagine there's going to be ways to reduce Blood Potency permanently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-10-2016, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:26:17-07:00","id":985183,"title":"","content":"Excellent - I don't have to feel like I'm filling a quota.<br /> <br /> So it sounds like new PCs would be about 1-10 years embraced?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:33:24-07:00","id":985189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985165-kindred-demographics-age-of-pcs?p=985183#post985183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent - I don't have to feel like I'm filling a quota.<br /> <br /> So it sounds like new PCs would be about 1-10 years embraced?</div> </div> </div> </div>1-49 (to keep at Blood Potency 1), I'd think. Depends on how &quot;current&quot; you want them to be. For a twist, you can also run them as far old, but recently out of Torpor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:38:27-07:00","id":985192,"title":"","content":"If a 50-150 year character has 15 xp it sounds like a character with 49 years as a kindred might have 10 or 15, just going by the guideline in the rulebook.<br /> <br /> If anyone wants to be recently awakened from torpor I'll probably go with that, although I'm not sure I expect anyone to go there.<br /> <br /> Blood potency can increase via xp expenditure as well as age and diablerie, and I assume anyone starting with higher potency is getting there by way of XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-10-2016, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T22:41:17-07:00","id":985277,"title":"","content":"The 1st edition core book said 1:50,000 was a very rough average, but more densely populated areas tend to have more Kindred per human and more rural areas tend to have fewer. That figure was never mentioned again, and in 2e not only does it not say anything of the sort, there is a lot of variety in the sample domains' population sizes.<br /> <br /> As for age, I like to say that starting characters with no Experiences are less than 150, since 3 is the highest Blood Potency you can start with without spending Experiences and it increases roughly at a rate of 1 every 50 years. But, there are guidelines for starting characters off with bonus Experiences, so you can start with Ancillae or Elders if you want, and it's easy enough to excuse starting characters being outside the rough 0-150 range if you want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T05:30:23-07:00","id":985360,"title":"","content":"Thanks much. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T10:21:33-07:00","id":986828,"title":"","content":"It depends on the domain and the 'story' you want to tell. In saying that, I don't mean a literal story - but the vibe you want to give when describing the setting to your players. A setting's population can create story seeds in the sense that an overpopulated domain could mean there's a vampire on every corner, bitterly fighting each other for territory, and there's multiple elders fighting for rule over a whole city. It would mean there's a lot more rank and file, a sense of hierarchy (e.g. prince, primogen council, sheriff, keeper of elysium, harpies, hounds). An undead society that interacts frequently. In an underpopulated city / town, I imagine that it'd be rare for vampires to see one another, everybody is pretty happy with their own, and hierarchies would be very, very basic (perhaps there's a rivalry between two lone elders who frequently pull the other four vampires in town and a bunch of ghouls into their plots against one another, perhaps one of them has a second-in-command that's their childe and the other has a younger vampire they've taken as a concubine - but that's as complex as the hierarchy gets on a cursory glance).<br /> <br /> I wouldn't worry too much about the exact populations. I'd just think about it in vague terms like the above, and using that as a springboard, start looking at the actual territory or play-space (the city your game is set in), then consider who claims what as their domain. Create some NPCs. When I create NPCs in well-populated cities (hierarchies included, a lot of my experience stemming more from Masquerade), I like to take heavy notice of their power levels compared to my players (not in the sense of how well they crush things with their bare hands, but to get a sense of the social dynamic that you're going to give your players when they interact with your NPCs - too many powerful NPCs means your PCs are going to be bullied, ignored, or treated in a really condescending fashion - and that's just not fun). I like to give PCs options and agency, and to do that, I like to make a variety of NPCs of differing power levels in comparison to the PCs - you need a few movers and shakers to create a seed for overarching plots (the guys who can bully your PCs without a thought), you need others at their level (rivals, those they can beat and outsmart or be beaten and outsmarted by in turn), and you need those that are simply below them (to give them a chance to help those weaker than them or potentially bully, a moral dilemma). All this depends on the PCs' ages, because a fresh embrace is going to be just as bullied by a 100 year old as much as a 300 year old vampire. Their rivals are going to be their peers, other freshly embraced vampires. Those below them are ghouls, mortals, failed / laughingstocks of vampires.<br /> <br /> When I create a vampire NPC, I think about their social circle, branching out - think about any vampires that may serve them, think about any ghouls that may serve them, think about any unknowing mortal servants, think about the social clique they flit around (high society parties, biker bars, music festivals, goth clubs), and think about where their public domain / haven is located (why, how?) - all in vague terms. I can't be stuffed being too exact with populations and preparing too many fully-written up NPCs, simply too much work. I will have my basics prepared in detail, and if I need to introduce a new NPC, I can introduce them on the fly - and if they happen to become important, and that's a frequency - then I can give them a more detailed look-over as the game demands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 10-13-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T12:19:22-07:00","id":986885,"title":"","content":"Thanks much - this is pretty solid advice, and helped me crystallize some of the things I've been thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T04:41:02-07:00","id":988784,"title":"","content":"With the way torpor works in Requiem, could a character of &quot;Starting&quot; xp level of skills and abilities be just about any age? If a vampire stayed in torpor long enough, wouldn't even an ancient vampire end up with stats the same as a freshly embraced neonate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T05:08:41-07:00","id":988796,"title":"","content":"Yes. There's a few of these in Ancient Mysteries. One from ancient Egypt, 1373 BCE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T05:13:32-07:00","id":988799,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head, I thought that 1% of the population being vampires would be good. I think a general scale of (1%)-(.01% ) of the human population would be a good scale of supernatural population. Plenty of supernaturals, while able to stay secret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12556,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","user":"Salsacookies","date":". 10-17-2016, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T05:53:30-07:00","id":988812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985165-kindred-demographics-age-of-pcs?p=988784#post988784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the way torpor works in Requiem, could a character of &quot;Starting&quot; xp level of skills and abilities be just about any age? If a vampire stayed in torpor long enough, wouldn't even an ancient vampire end up with stats the same as a freshly embraced neonate?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e, you only lose blood potency in torpor, nothing else. An ancient vampire with traits appropriate to an ancient vampire will keep those traits even in torpor.<br /> <br /> An ancient that's only been active for a few years before going into torpor could end up with the same traits as a freshly embraced neonate because they were a freshly embraced neonate all along, but a genuine elder would keep their elder level traits.<br /> <br /> Like if someone in my group wants to play such a character we'd probably work <i>something</i> out so as to get a satisfactory result.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should read Ancient Mysteries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-17-2016, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T10:17:26-07:00","id":988913,"title":"","content":"2e does have that sidebar about how sometimes vampires wake up from Torpor having lost all of their memories. I have allowed players to justify very old vampires with starting experience using that sidebar as justification. That does mean playing an amnesia story, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T12:15:55-07:00","id":988972,"title":"","content":"Where's the sidebar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T12:50:17-07:00","id":988985,"title":"","content":"I don't think hard and fast ratios suit the ChroD in general. Every city is unique and disconnected from most other cities. That said, as a general rule of thumb, vampire population scales to mortal population, and competition scales to population density. You can manageably cap your vampire population by assuming that they aren't squabbling simply over feeding rights but also over local power and influence.<br /> <br /> When building my city, I adopted a method of breaking the environment down into neighborhoods, identifying the defining force of that neighborhood, and using that as a barometer to determine the general population. So I have an Invictus Prince Pro Tempore who's a real estate maven and who's seat of power is the financial/tourism corridor. This is a region where domain right are likely to be fairly strict, so I expanded out what sort of bureaucratic positions would be necessary for this region, sprinkled in some powerful kindred who don't have a direct role in the government but have the influence to maintain penthouses, and added a few vassals and others who are flying under the radar. As such, you have these hubs of control that stretch a few blocks and are the sole domain of a single kindred or a kindred family and then these gaps between the spaces where aspiring or struggling vampires can slip between the cracks. Apart from the core of the tourist hub and the airport district which are tightly overseen, lords and ladies are largely required to monitor their territory themselves. It's a medium density neighborhood.<br /> <br /> Then I looked at Emory University. It's a college neighborhood that houses both prominent hospitals and the CDC headquarters. This means that it's both ideal hunting grounds for predators and a place of concern for the establishment. Supernatural violations will be treated with extreme prejudice by mortal authorities. As such, it's tightly controlled by a small group of Ordo Dracul and closely monitored by the sheriff. Unaccepted incursions into the area are largely treated as capital offenses. As a result, it's a very low density and homogenized neighborhood.<br /> <br /> On the far end of the spectrum, you have Southwest Atlanta, an expansive spread of the city that's traditionally black and low income and also disproportionately high in terms of its presence of churches and other religious institutions. There's a high population and a low lack of non-herd resources, which makes it a high density neighborhood for vampires. It also has a disproportionate amount of Sanctum influence, and the LS in my city tends to maintain large flocks of kindred believers. As such, characters who venture into this stretch of the city are more likely to encounter baronies that shift every couple of blocks and see communal broods overseeing territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T13:14:49-07:00","id":988993,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8492\" data-vbnamecard=\"8492\">dxanders</a> Yes, that is probably the route I'm going to take. I need to sit down with a map of the greater Seattle area and mark up neighborhoods and such to get it going. Right now I'll just aim to create the vampires who are relevant and add more as needed. It'll probably be a couple of months before this gets off the ground, so I do have some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T13:24:46-07:00","id":988995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985165-kindred-demographics-age-of-pcs?p=988972#post988972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's the sidebar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I guess I misremembered, it's not a sidebar, it's just in the text about Torpor on page 105.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> During her slumber, she experiences strange, nonsensical dreams that keep her mind active and exercised. Usually, this means she\u2019s prepared to adapt to a new world. Sometimes, this goes awry; she wakes up a whole new person, or, rarely, with distorted memories of her past existence. </div> </div> </div>So I will allow players to take some creative liberty from that passage and play a tabula rasa character who woke up with no memories and starting exp after a long-duration Torpor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T13:37:14-07:00","id":989000,"title":"","content":"Ah, fair enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T21:55:57-07:00","id":989200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985165-kindred-demographics-age-of-pcs?p=988995#post988995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I guess I misremembered, it's not a sidebar, it's just in the text about Torpor on page 105.<br /> <br /> So I will allow players to take some creative liberty from that passage and play a tabula rasa character who woke up with no memories and starting exp after a long-duration Torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I agree with no memory but an ancient with strenght 5-6, Vigor 3-4, Majesty 5 or whatever she had, it's quite weird that she wake up without any of this ability. Maybe she could not remember to have them but I'd say she'll discover to have a superhuman strenght (passive), speed and ability to bend emotions quite soon. But this is just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T22:09:33-07:00","id":989203,"title":"","content":"I imagine Kindred survival rates are sort of like ancient mortal survival rates; survive your early years and you're pretty likely to make it far. If you've made it to 200 or so, it's by not making the kind of mistakes most likely to get you destroyed in the next thousand years too. So there's a likely bubble of young Kindred who've been Embraced by also relatively young Kindred, and then a gap, and then a decent population of subtle elders who spend some time torpid or relatively divorced from mortal affairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:11:14-07:00","id":989446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985165-kindred-demographics-age-of-pcs?p=989200#post989200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I agree with no memory but an ancient with strenght 5-6, Vigor 3-4, Majesty 5 or whatever she had, it's quite weird that she wake up without any of this ability. Maybe she could not remember to have them but I'd say she'll discover to have a superhuman strenght (passive), speed and ability to bend emotions quite soon. But this is just my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the vampire body is static, so increases in strength might have a literal 'Will to Power'. If that will is linked to identity, and identity to belief, perhaps jumbling a vampires memories and other self beliefs would weaken their will. Plus, because BP takes a dive, the beast isn't as strong either, so relying on it would lead to a weaker vampire as well. As you said, that it doesn't make sense is your opinion and I don't wish to suggest that you must presume this about vampires, but as a reasonable account of why a confused elder doesn't have their strength, while a more focused one does, I find it appealing and present it to you for consideration. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:20:53-07:00","id":989452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985165-kindred-demographics-age-of-pcs?p=989200#post989200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I agree with no memory but an ancient with strenght 5-6, Vigor 3-4, Majesty 5 or whatever she had, it's quite weird that she wake up without any of this ability. Maybe she could not remember to have them but I'd say she'll discover to have a superhuman strenght (passive), speed and ability to bend emotions quite soon. But this is just my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but if I have a player who wants to play an old vampire despite the fact that we're starting fresh or at low exp, and is ok with playing an amnesiac, I think this is a perfectly fine way to justify that narratively. You can always say that spending Experiences to buy up your Attributes, Disciplines, Skills, Merits, etc. is not actually learning new abilities but &quot;remembering&quot; ones you forgot you already had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:41:21-07:00","id":989464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985165-kindred-demographics-age-of-pcs?p=988995#post988995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I guess I misremembered, it's not a sidebar, it's just in the text about Torpor on page 105.<br /> <br /> So I will allow players to take some creative liberty from that passage and play a tabula rasa character who woke up with no memories and starting exp after a long-duration Torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Priority #1: Find a Touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}